# arvo-sparse, backlog

> **Type-surface reminder**: new entries use `arvo::USize` /
> `Bool` / `UFixed<N, 0, S>` instead of `usize` / `bool` / `u*`;
> `notko::Maybe` / `Outcome` instead of `Option` / `Result`. See
> `rules/type-surface.md`.

Round 202605111719 lifted every algorithm to W-generic at the public
surface. Wider-than-64 adjacency works out of the box for any
`W: BitPrim` the consumer picks, and CSR-shaped adjacency drives the
same algorithms through the `SparseAdjacency` trait family. BACKLOG
entries below name only items not yet shipped.

## SpMV

Sparse matrix-vector multiply patterns. Deferred per the original
design. Same representation and API surface as the above algorithms;
add when a concrete consumer need surfaces.

## arvo-graph W-generic sweep

`arvo-graph` carries the same `Bits<64, Hot, Unsigned>` hardcoding in
`topo_sort`, `upward_rank`, `downward_rank`, `longest_path`,
`components`, `waist_detect`, `spanning_tree`. Tracked in the
workspace audit at round 202605111741; lands as a follow-up round
opening after the current sparse + spectral round closes.
